And if you exaggerate
the threat in your head,

00:25:25.724 --> 00:25:27.792 align:start size:84% position:16%
you are then willing
to take actions

00:25:27.792 --> 00:25:29.261
that you otherwise would not,

00:25:29.261 --> 00:25:30.996
and violate principles that
you otherwise would not.

00:25:30.996 --> 00:25:33.798 align:start size:88% position:13%
And we saw this as,
you know, during COVID.

00:25:33.798 --> 00:25:35.033
People get scared.

00:25:35.033 --> 00:25:37.068
People overestimate the
nature of the threat,

00:25:37.068 --> 00:25:39.304
and then the reaction they
demand from their government

00:25:39.304 --> 00:25:42.807
or they themselves have is
just completely out of whack.

00:25:42.807 --> 00:25:46.811
And so destroying democracy
to prevent Donald Trump,

00:25:46.811 --> 00:25:50.048 align:start size:88% position:13%
that doesn't make sense
to me, personally.

00:25:50.048 --> 00:25:51.550
- Right.

00:25:51.550 --> 00:25:52.817
So let's talk about the
COVID thing a little bit,

00:25:52.817 --> 00:25:54.920
because obviously it has
framed almost everything

00:25:54.920 --> 00:25:57.222
over the last couple of years.

00:25:57.222 --> 00:26:00.992 align:start size:97% position:3%
I went radically
anti-mandate and pro-freedom.

00:26:00.992 --> 00:26:03.728
Literally moved my entire
life across the country

00:26:03.728 --> 00:26:06.665
in the midst of it because
of all of the craziness.

00:26:08.099 --> 00:26:10.835
I sense you're in a similar
spot when it came to mandates

00:26:10.835 --> 00:26:12.337
and things of that matter.

00:26:12.337 --> 00:26:14.706
But what was your evolution
like, related to all that?

00:26:14.706 --> 00:26:17.375 align:start size:88% position:13%
- I supported the first
lockdown in the UK.

00:26:17.375 --> 00:26:19.611 align:start size:81% position:19%
We didn't know
what was going on.

00:26:19.611 --> 00:26:21.313
And we were told it
was very dangerous.

00:26:21.313 --> 00:26:24.149
And while we should all
be skeptical, of course,

00:26:24.149 --> 00:26:25.383 align:start size:84% position:16%
of what the mainstream
media tell us

00:26:25.383 --> 00:26:26.585
in that sort of situation.

00:26:26.585 --> 00:26:28.453 align:start size:84% position:16%
I do think, as a
responsible citizen,

00:26:28.453 --> 00:26:30.622
you do have a duty to
at least consider it.

00:26:30.622 --> 00:26:32.457
And remember, what we
were told in the UK

00:26:32.457 --> 00:26:34.426
it's just gonna be three weeks.

00:26:34.426 --> 00:26:35.560
We're gonna solve the problem.

00:26:35.560 --> 00:26:36.795
Everything's fine.

00:26:36.795 --> 00:26:37.996 align:start size:84% position:16%
- [Dave] Oh, they
told you three week?

00:26:37.996 --> 00:26:38.863 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Three weeks.
- We got two weeks.

00:26:38.863 --> 00:26:40.131
- Two weeks, right.

00:26:40.131 --> 00:26:41.333
- They told us either
two weeks or 15 days,

00:26:41.333 --> 00:26:42.534 align:start size:88% position:13%
they were always working
with one extra day.

00:26:42.534 --> 00:26:44.869 align:start size:88% position:13%
- The longest three
weeks in human history,

00:26:44.869 --> 00:26:46.271
those turned out to be.

00:26:46.271 --> 00:26:49.507 align:start size:97% position:3%
So in the beginning I
supported the first lockdown,

00:26:51.343 --> 00:26:54.613
you know, but from there,

00:26:54.613 --> 00:26:58.216
I just felt that we went
in a dystopian direction

00:26:58.216 --> 00:26:59.384
very, very quickly.

00:27:00.852 --> 00:27:03.722
And on the basis of data that
to me didn't seem reasonable,

00:27:03.722 --> 00:27:05.924 align:start size:84% position:16%
we were forced to wear
these face nappies

00:27:05.924 --> 00:27:08.660 align:start size:84% position:16%
that don't do
anything as we know.

00:27:08.660 --> 00:27:11.396 align:start size:97% position:3%
And not only do we know that
now, we knew that before.

00:27:11.396 --> 00:27:12.998
We knew that before. Right?

00:27:12.998 --> 00:27:15.600
And I think it signals to me

00:27:15.600 --> 00:27:18.737
something I talk about
in the book, actually,

00:27:18.737 --> 00:27:21.473
that we are importing
ways of doing business

00:27:21.473 --> 00:27:23.241 align:start size:84% position:16%
that are fundamentally
anti-western.

00:27:23.241 --> 00:27:25.677
And we have this from the UK.

00:27:25.677 --> 00:27:29.247
Neil Ferguson, not the
historian who we love.

00:27:29.247 --> 00:27:30.482
- [Dave] Yeah.

00:27:30.482 --> 00:27:32.083
- But the guy who
was essentially

00:27:32.083 --> 00:27:34.386 align:start size:97% position:3%
behind advising the government
to have the lockdowns,

00:27:34.386 --> 00:27:36.254
he was a scientist in the UK.

00:27:36.254 --> 00:27:37.889 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Oh, that must have been
tough for our Niall Ferguson.

00:27:37.889 --> 00:27:39.190 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah, I imagine so.
- Oh man!

00:27:39.190 --> 00:27:43.361 align:start size:88% position:13%
- So he said in, I think
it's a Times article,

00:27:43.361 --> 00:27:46.498 align:start size:88% position:13%
that we didn't know
lockdowns were possible

00:27:46.498 --> 00:27:48.667
until we saw what the
Chinese were doing.

00:27:48.667 --> 00:27:50.568
- I mean, what a horrific...

00:27:50.568 --> 00:27:53.038 align:start size:97% position:3%
- And I think this speaks
to something else, you know,

00:27:53.038 --> 00:27:55.807 align:start size:88% position:13%
one of the things I
mentioned in the book is

00:27:55.807 --> 00:27:57.275
most people don't,

00:27:57.275 --> 00:27:58.510 align:start size:97% position:3%
do you know where political
correctness comes from?

00:27:58.510 --> 00:27:59.678
The term itself?

00:27:59.678 --> 00:28:00.979 align:start size:84% position:16%
- The term political
correctness?

00:28:00.979 --> 00:28:02.347
- [Konstantin] Yeah.

00:28:02.347 --> 00:28:03.181
- I don't think so.

00:28:03.181 --> 00:28:04.282
- The Soviet Union.

00:28:04.282 --> 00:28:05.717
And it never had anything to do

00:28:05.717 --> 00:28:07.786
with protecting the
rights of minorities

00:28:07.786 --> 00:28:10.221 align:start size:84% position:16%
and not offending
people or being nice

00:28:10.221 --> 00:28:11.322
or anything like that.

00:28:11.322 --> 00:28:12.724
It was a very simple thing,

00:28:12.724 --> 00:28:14.626 align:start size:81% position:19%
to tell people,
like my ancestors,

00:28:14.626 --> 00:28:16.628
"Comrade, this may
be factually correct,

00:28:16.628 --> 00:28:18.630 align:start size:84% position:16%
but it is politically
incorrect."

00:28:18.630 --> 00:28:19.864
And what that means is,

00:28:19.864 --> 00:28:23.101
you are not adhering to
the party line, right?

00:28:23.101 --> 00:28:25.537 align:start size:84% position:16%
And to me, the fact
that we adopted

00:28:25.537 --> 00:28:29.941
a Chinese style response
to that sort of threat

00:28:29.941 --> 00:28:34.546
signals that we are moving in
an authoritarian direction.

00:28:34.546 --> 00:28:36.614
And the thing that scared
me most, this is, look,

00:28:36.614 --> 00:28:40.652 align:start size:97% position:3%
this is not a popular thing
to say, but I think it's true,

00:28:40.652 --> 00:28:42.420
at least in our country.

00:28:43.688 --> 00:28:45.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
It wasn't the politicians
that did this.

00:28:45.857 --> 00:28:47.025
It was the people.

00:28:47.025 --> 00:28:48.359
They wanted this.

00:28:48.359 --> 00:28:51.062 align:start size:84% position:16%
Poll after poll, after
poll, after poll.

00:28:51.062 --> 00:28:53.765
You know, 20% of people
want nightclubs shut down

00:28:53.765 --> 00:28:57.502 align:start size:84% position:16%
permanently,
irrespective of COVID,

00:28:57.502 --> 00:28:59.671
irrespective of COVID, Dave.

00:28:59.671 --> 00:29:00.939
They wanna shut down things,

00:29:00.939 --> 00:29:03.975
just because there's an
opportunity to do so.

00:29:03.975 --> 00:29:07.846 align:start position:0%
Wear masks on public
transport, 40% or 30%, forever,

00:29:07.846 --> 00:29:09.447
doesn't matter if there's COVID.

00:29:10.615 --> 00:29:12.117
You know, we shat the bed.

00:29:12.117 --> 00:29:15.019 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I'm really uncomfortable
with what happened.

00:29:15.019 --> 00:29:16.654
- You know what
day it was for me

00:29:16.654 --> 00:29:19.891
that I realized what nonsense
it was, 'cause I'm with you.

00:29:19.891 --> 00:29:22.227 align:start size:97% position:3%
The first two weeks I granted
everybody a long leash.

00:29:22.227 --> 00:29:23.728 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I can even
grant, in retrospect,

00:29:23.728 --> 00:29:24.929
I can even grant a longer leash.

00:29:24.929 --> 00:29:26.164
We were so hit in the head.

00:29:26.164 --> 00:29:28.032
It was the first time
we had dealt with this.

00:29:28.032 --> 00:29:29.534
I think we've all learned a lot

00:29:29.534 --> 00:29:32.337 align:start position:0%
and hopefully a certain portion
of us won't do it again.

00:29:32.337 --> 00:29:34.038
But for me it really was day 15.

00:29:34.038 --> 00:29:35.874 align:start size:88% position:13%
Once they said two weeks
to stop the spread,

00:29:35.874 --> 00:29:39.577
and we rolled into day 15,
'cause it changed overnight.

00:29:39.577 --> 00:29:41.246
They kept saying the new normal.

00:29:41.246 --> 00:29:43.915
And once I started hearing
the new normal everywhere,

00:29:43.915 --> 00:29:46.317 align:start size:84% position:16%
it was on commercials,
it was on NBC, CNN,

00:29:46.317 --> 00:29:47.919
I was like, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:29:47.919 --> 00:29:49.454
Something else is going on here.

00:29:49.454 --> 00:29:51.256
And then that clearly
bore out to be true.

00:29:51.256 --> 00:29:53.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
But what do you think that
says about human nature

00:29:53.958 --> 00:29:56.795 align:start size:88% position:13%
or the spiritual side
of what's going on here?

00:29:56.795 --> 00:29:58.129
That we actually wanted it.

00:29:58.129 --> 00:29:59.831 align:start size:84% position:16%
And from an American
perspective,

00:29:59.831 --> 00:30:02.167
I don't know if this is quite
true from a UK perspective,

00:30:02.167 --> 00:30:03.668
we've re-voted,

00:30:03.668 --> 00:30:05.069
we voted in a lot of the
same people that did this.

00:30:05.069 --> 00:30:08.406 align:start position:0%
Gretchen Whitmer, Gavin Newsom,
the list goes on and on.

00:30:09.607 --> 00:30:11.109
- Well, we know this
throughout history.

00:30:11.109 --> 00:30:14.312
I sort of joked during the
pandemic at some point that,

00:30:14.312 --> 00:30:17.448
you know, this is at
least the one thing

00:30:17.448 --> 00:30:18.683
that hasn't happened yet,

00:30:18.683 --> 00:30:20.118
is that we haven't
blamed the Jews.

00:30:20.118 --> 00:30:22.353
But we did just
about everything,

00:30:22.353 --> 00:30:24.255 align:start size:88% position:13%
It was just about
everything else, right?

00:30:24.255 --> 00:30:26.024
So when people are
scared, when people,

00:30:26.024 --> 00:30:29.561
when bad things are going
on, people, you know, they,

00:30:29.561 --> 00:30:32.330
the instincts come out and
their worst side comes out.

00:30:32.330 --> 00:30:33.832
And it's like human
beings, you know,

00:30:33.832 --> 00:30:36.434
only on an individual level,
when you're having a bad day,

00:30:36.434 --> 00:30:39.370 align:start size:97% position:3%
all your worst aspects of
your personality are magnified

00:30:39.370 --> 00:30:40.972 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the best ones
are dampened, right?

00:30:40.972 --> 00:30:43.441 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I tell you
what it was for me.

00:30:43.441 --> 00:30:48.413 align:start size:97% position:3%
For me it was what
happened over BLM in the UK

00:30:49.881 --> 00:30:53.418
that really showed me that
this is a complete nonsense.

00:30:53.418 --> 00:30:57.088 align:start size:88% position:13%
Because we had this
first lockdown, which I,

00:30:57.088 --> 00:31:00.525
and almost everybody
obeyed to the letter,

00:31:00.525 --> 00:31:02.093
and had a lot of respect for.

00:31:03.494 --> 00:31:05.763 align:start size:97% position:3%
There was another moment
when the sun first came out,

00:31:05.763 --> 00:31:08.099 align:start size:84% position:16%
it's a rare
occurrence in England.

00:31:08.099 --> 00:31:12.303 align:start position:0%
And some people had the temerity
to go outside and sunbathe.

00:31:12.303 --> 00:31:13.571
- My God.

00:31:13.571 --> 00:31:16.007
- And this was, by this
point it was very clear

00:31:16.007 --> 00:31:18.877 align:start size:88% position:13%
that this virus does not
spread well outdoors.

00:31:18.877 --> 00:31:21.179 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I said on Twitter
that, you know,

00:31:21.179 --> 00:31:23.815
I think people should be
allowed to sunbathe and I,

00:31:23.815 --> 00:31:25.250
it was, I,

00:31:25.250 --> 00:31:27.385
I don't know what I
could compare it to,

00:31:27.385 --> 00:31:28.820
the reaction that I got.

00:31:28.820 --> 00:31:30.355 align:start size:97% position:3%
So I thought people were
starting to lose their minds.

00:31:30.355 --> 00:31:32.423
But then we saw
the whole country

00:31:32.423 --> 00:31:35.126
having been locked down
for this entire time.

00:31:37.195 --> 00:31:38.696
BLM happens.

00:31:38.696 --> 00:31:41.733
And suddenly protests
outside without masks

00:31:41.733 --> 00:31:43.868 align:start size:84% position:16%
are a public health
intervention?

00:31:43.868 --> 00:31:45.403
- They were actually
pro-public health.

00:31:45.403 --> 00:31:46.671 align:start size:97% position:3%
That's what we were told here-
- They had to be-

00:31:46.671 --> 00:31:48.039 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Because racism was
a bigger problem.

00:31:48.039 --> 00:31:49.440 align:start size:97% position:3%
- They're to be celebrated.
- Yeah.

00:31:49.440 --> 00:31:50.909
- They're to be encouraged.

00:31:52.644 --> 00:31:55.446
If you want to live in a
western liberal democracy

00:31:55.446 --> 00:31:57.482
in which people are
judged on the content

00:31:57.482 --> 00:32:00.585
of their character,
that can't happen.

00:32:01.653 --> 00:32:02.921
That can't happen.

00:32:02.921 --> 00:32:05.623
And to me, that was the
moment when I just went,

00:32:05.623 --> 00:32:07.358
okay, this is done.

00:32:07.358 --> 00:32:10.194 align:start size:88% position:13%
And to the point where,
you know, we were,

00:32:10.194 --> 00:32:13.298
I remember going to
speaking at a protest

00:32:13.298 --> 00:32:14.565
in Parliament Square,

00:32:14.565 --> 00:32:17.635
outside the Houses of
Parliament in London,

00:32:18.836 --> 00:32:21.339
when they were trying
to force medical staff

00:32:21.339 --> 00:32:25.109
to have a vaccine in order
to remain in their post.

00:32:26.844 --> 00:32:29.948 align:start position:0%
And it's interesting, I've
never told this story publicly,

00:32:29.948 --> 00:32:32.417 align:start size:84% position:16%
or maybe, no, I
don't think I have.

00:32:32.417 --> 00:32:33.985
When my wife gave birth,

00:32:33.985 --> 00:32:36.120
she had quite a long
and difficult labor.

00:32:36.120 --> 00:32:37.355 align:start size:84% position:16%
And it was supposed
to be at home.

00:32:37.355 --> 00:32:38.823 align:start size:81% position:19%
She wanted to give
birth at home.

00:32:38.823 --> 00:32:41.292
But we had to go to to hospital
'cause it wasn't going well.

00:32:41.292 --> 00:32:44.762
And it was a long and
difficult and scary

00:32:44.762 --> 00:32:45.930
and all the rest of it.

00:32:45.930 --> 00:32:48.066 align:start size:84% position:16%
But as it was looking
like, you know,

00:32:48.066 --> 00:32:51.436 align:start size:97% position:3%
things were gonna get really
bad, this midwife came in

00:32:51.436 --> 00:32:53.738 align:start size:97% position:3%
who was a higher level
midwife than the other ones.

00:32:53.738 --> 00:32:56.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she was like this
angel, she was incredible.

00:32:56.641 --> 00:32:59.177
And she helped my wife
to give birth naturally.

00:32:59.177 --> 00:33:01.479 align:start size:84% position:16%
It was just like,
she fixed the thing.

00:33:01.479 --> 00:33:04.148
It was beautiful.
It was amazing.

00:33:04.148 --> 00:33:06.284
And afterwards, all the
other midwives had left

00:33:06.284 --> 00:33:07.685 align:start size:84% position:16%
and she was just
filling out some forms

00:33:07.685 --> 00:33:09.120
and she was asking
us various questions.

00:33:09.120 --> 00:33:10.989
And my wife who was
pregnant at the time,

00:33:10.989 --> 00:33:13.124
the vaccine came out,
wasn't gonna have it.

00:33:14.859 --> 00:33:17.128
And this midwife was
reading the thing.

00:33:17.128 --> 00:33:18.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
She goes, oh, this,
asking various questions.

00:33:18.830 --> 00:33:21.666
Then she said, "Are
you vaccinated?"

00:33:21.666 --> 00:33:25.069
And I, you know, I, my
wife's just given birth,

00:33:25.069 --> 00:33:26.371
I'm sort of trying
to look after her.

00:33:26.371 --> 00:33:29.907 align:start size:84% position:16%
I don't want it to,
you know, but equally,

00:33:29.907 --> 00:33:32.210
I don't want, you know,
this medical professional

00:33:32.210 --> 00:33:34.512 align:start size:88% position:13%
to think that we are
the wackos and whatever.

00:33:34.512 --> 00:33:35.780
- [Dave] Yeah yeah yeah.

00:33:35.780 --> 00:33:37.882
- So I said, "Well, you
know, we were pregnant",

00:33:37.882 --> 00:33:40.218 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I start sort of
fumbling for an answer

00:33:40.218 --> 00:33:44.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
that will please both
sides, which is unlike me.

00:33:44.088 --> 00:33:47.458
And she said, "Oh, don't
worry, I'm not vaccinated."

00:33:50.228 --> 00:33:51.763
And we had a conversation.

00:33:51.763 --> 00:33:55.066 align:start size:88% position:13%
I said, "So you must
have, you must have not,

00:33:55.066 --> 00:33:56.868
you must have felt really
bad when the government

00:33:56.868 --> 00:34:00.238 align:start size:84% position:16%
was trying to force
you to be vaccinated?"

00:34:00.238 --> 00:34:02.607
And she said, "I
was gonna quit."

00:34:02.607 --> 00:34:04.509
That woman would
not have been there

00:34:04.509 --> 00:34:07.378 align:start size:97% position:3%
if the government had
carried on with that program.

00:34:07.378 --> 00:34:10.014
And so for all the crap we took

00:34:10.014 --> 00:34:12.717
for standing up on that issue,

00:34:12.717 --> 00:34:15.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
I felt that to me was
the ultimate vindication,

00:34:15.553 --> 00:34:16.854
that that happened.

00:34:16.854 --> 00:34:20.158
It's a story that
I really appreciate

00:34:20.158 --> 00:34:22.193
and think about a lot, you know,

00:34:22.193 --> 00:34:23.661
and that's when, you know,

00:34:23.661 --> 00:34:25.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
we talked about being
brave and whatever, just,

00:34:25.897 --> 00:34:27.365
it's nonsense.

00:34:27.365 --> 00:34:28.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
We just gotta, we all
gotta say what we believe.

00:34:28.599 --> 00:34:30.301 align:start size:84% position:16%
- So since the woke
thing is kind of what,

00:34:30.301 --> 00:34:32.470 align:start size:88% position:13%
what I think has really
put you on the map,

00:34:32.470 --> 00:34:35.706 align:start size:84% position:16%
do you see the
precursor to COVID,

00:34:35.706 --> 00:34:37.108
with all of the woke craziness

00:34:37.108 --> 00:34:39.243
that we were dealing
with before COVID,

00:34:39.243 --> 00:34:40.511
then COVID comes,

00:34:40.511 --> 00:34:42.647
now everyone's brains
are completely broken.

00:34:42.647 --> 00:34:45.683
Does it seem like sort
of fairly obvious to you

00:34:45.683 --> 00:34:48.019
that we're at where
we're at right now?

00:34:48.019 --> 00:34:50.221 align:start size:88% position:13%
That if you had three
years or whatever we had

00:34:50.221 --> 00:34:52.256
of like hardcore
wokeness online,

00:34:52.256 --> 00:34:54.325
then we get three
years of COVID,

00:34:54.325 --> 00:34:57.929
and now we're just in
this like post COVID,

00:34:57.929 --> 00:35:00.298
woke broken weirdness.

00:35:00.298 --> 00:35:02.667
- Yeah, I think COVID broke
a lot of people's brains,

00:35:02.667 --> 00:35:03.835
left and right.

00:35:03.835 --> 00:35:06.537
Because you and I both know,

00:35:06.537 --> 00:35:07.772
social media's not good for you.

00:35:07.772 --> 00:35:09.307
And we all spent three years

00:35:09.307 --> 00:35:11.709 align:start size:88% position:13%
just downloading
Twitter into our heads.

00:35:11.709 --> 00:35:13.077
A lot of people did.

00:35:13.077 --> 00:35:15.079
So I think that's
had a huge impact.

00:35:15.079 --> 00:35:17.482 align:start size:84% position:16%
But I think the
bigger question is,

00:35:19.150 --> 00:35:21.185 align:start size:84% position:16%
we don't have a shared
consensus anymore.

00:35:22.487 --> 00:35:23.721
We don't.

00:35:23.721 --> 00:35:26.691 align:start size:88% position:13%
And how can you, how can
you have a, you know,

00:35:26.691 --> 00:35:29.894
you talk about classical
liberalism, that means,

00:35:29.894 --> 00:35:31.429
part of that means the ability

00:35:31.429 --> 00:35:33.664
to discuss ideas
and debate ideas.

00:35:33.664 --> 00:35:36.968
How can you debate ideas if
you don't agree on reality?

00:35:36.968 --> 00:35:39.570
Right? There is no
basis in reality.

00:35:39.570 --> 00:35:41.105
And I actually, it's
interesting because,

00:35:41.105 --> 00:35:43.608
I don't know if you
saw Gavin Newsom's

00:35:43.608 --> 00:35:46.210 align:start size:84% position:16%
non-campaign campaign
ads recently?

00:35:46.210 --> 00:35:47.345
- Oh, I saw them.
- You saw that.

00:35:47.345 --> 00:35:48.279
- We played them.

00:35:48.279 --> 00:35:49.547
I don't know if you know this,

00:35:49.547 --> 00:35:51.182
I don't like that guy-
- Yeah, I imagine so.

00:35:51.182 --> 00:35:54.819
But what I found interesting
about that is, he was using

00:35:54.819 --> 00:35:59.323 align:start size:97% position:3%
all the, quote unquote,
tropes of people on the right.

00:35:59.323 --> 00:36:03.661 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so he's basically saying,
"I believe in freedom."

00:36:03.661 --> 00:36:05.163
- No, it's incredible,

00:36:05.163 --> 00:36:07.031
that he has the gall to put
any of this in his mouth,

00:36:07.031 --> 00:36:09.000 align:start position:0%
it's incredible, and everyone's
the reverse of the truth.

00:36:09.000 --> 00:36:10.868
We went through the list.

00:36:10.868 --> 00:36:12.103
- Right.

00:36:12.103 --> 00:36:14.172 align:start size:84% position:16%
But there are people
who believe that.

00:36:14.172 --> 00:36:15.339 align:start size:84% position:16%
And there are people
on the other side

00:36:15.339 --> 00:36:17.008
who believe the opposite.

00:36:17.008 --> 00:36:18.442
And so that lack
of shared consensus

00:36:18.442 --> 00:36:19.777
is really where
the problem's at.

00:36:19.777 --> 00:36:21.579
- So you got a solution on that?

00:36:21.579 --> 00:36:22.947
What do you, I mean, I talk
about this all the time,

00:36:22.947 --> 00:36:24.448
what do we do about that?

00:36:24.448 --> 00:36:27.585
I mean, I know, I think it
was a very tactical move

00:36:27.585 --> 00:36:29.120
that Gavin did that,

00:36:29.120 --> 00:36:32.323
to use the words freedom to
talk about all of the things

00:36:32.323 --> 00:36:34.759 align:start size:97% position:3%
that are happening in Florida
as if they're negative

00:36:34.759 --> 00:36:36.561 align:start size:84% position:16%
relative to freedom.
- Yeah.

00:36:36.561 --> 00:36:39.030
- And that we're the ones
banning books. Not true.

00:36:39.030 --> 00:36:41.732
It's actually him trying to
find "To Kill a Mockingbird"

00:36:41.732 --> 00:36:43.568
in California state schools.

00:36:43.568 --> 00:36:44.769
All of these things, you know,

00:36:44.769 --> 00:36:46.437 align:start size:81% position:19%
women's rights
and your own body.

00:36:46.437 --> 00:36:47.838
It's like, "Wait,
you were the one

00:36:47.838 --> 00:36:49.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
trying to inject everybody
with your stuff."

00:36:49.740 --> 00:36:51.342
You know, all the nonsense.

00:36:51.342 --> 00:36:52.410
But what do we do with that,

00:36:52.410 --> 00:36:54.679
as that continues to break down?

00:36:54.679 --> 00:36:55.513
- Well...

00:36:56.981 --> 00:37:00.585 align:start size:97% position:3%
I oscillate between two
different thoughts on this.

00:37:00.585 --> 00:37:04.589 align:start position:0%
I've talked a lot about the
post-woke future because to me,

00:37:04.589 --> 00:37:09.594 align:start position:0%
a lot of the people who I would
hope were on our side once,

00:37:10.962 --> 00:37:12.964 align:start size:97% position:3%
I see them as equally
abominable now, as the woke.

00:37:12.964 --> 00:37:15.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
The anti-woke is becoming
a parody of itself.

00:37:17.235 --> 00:37:19.237
- What would be an
example of that?

00:37:20.504 --> 00:37:22.607
- There are many
examples of that.

00:37:22.607 --> 00:37:24.976
I mean, there are a lot of
people on the anti-woke side

00:37:24.976 --> 00:37:26.744
who don't believe
in free speech.

00:37:26.744 --> 00:37:28.913 align:start size:88% position:13%
They don't believe in
debating people's ideas.

00:37:28.913 --> 00:37:31.182 align:start size:81% position:19%
They believe in
destroying people.

00:37:31.182 --> 00:37:33.451 align:start size:88% position:13%
There are a lot of
people who are unwilling

00:37:33.451 --> 00:37:35.419
to have a discussion with
somebody they disagree,

00:37:35.419 --> 00:37:37.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they spend their
entire time owning people.

00:37:37.922 --> 00:37:40.458
Now look, I go on the BBC
and make them look bad

00:37:40.458 --> 00:37:41.392
and we'll put a clip out.

00:37:41.392 --> 00:37:42.893
But I, that's not,

00:37:42.893 --> 00:37:44.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's not who I am and
it's not what I do, right?

00:37:44.729 --> 00:37:45.663
- Yeah.

00:37:45.663 --> 00:37:47.465
- And I think generally,

00:37:47.465 --> 00:37:49.767
look, it's hard to be anti,
we talked about earlier,

00:37:49.767 --> 00:37:52.903 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's hard to be anti
something and be constructive.

00:37:52.903 --> 00:37:54.405 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's hard, objectively.
- Yeah.

00:37:54.405 --> 00:37:56.774
- And so for me, the answer,

00:37:56.774 --> 00:38:00.344
when I talk about going
for a post-woke future,

00:38:00.344 --> 00:38:03.147 align:start size:88% position:13%
culturally at least,
what that means to me is

00:38:04.348 --> 00:38:06.050
I don't believe that,

00:38:06.050 --> 00:38:07.785
before we started, we
talked about the NBA.

00:38:07.785 --> 00:38:08.953
- Yeah.
- Right?

00:38:08.953 --> 00:38:10.588 align:start size:84% position:16%
Which was very
heavily politicized.

00:38:10.588 --> 00:38:12.356
I don't think the
average person,

00:38:12.356 --> 00:38:16.027 align:start size:88% position:13%
the average person,
wants to turn on the NBA

00:38:16.027 --> 00:38:19.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
and watch a bunch of
players talking about BLM.

00:38:19.263 --> 00:38:20.765
I also, by the way,

00:38:20.765 --> 00:38:22.767
don't think you want
to turn on the NBA

00:38:22.767 --> 00:38:24.702
and watch a bunch
of players talking

00:38:24.702 --> 00:38:29.173
about how CRT is destroying
schools and all of that.

00:38:29.173 --> 00:38:30.908
I have this strange feeling

00:38:30.908 --> 00:38:33.144
they wanna watch
some basketball.

00:38:33.144 --> 00:38:35.413
- Dribble the damn
ball. How about that?

00:38:35.413 --> 00:38:36.914
- Well, you know,

00:38:36.914 --> 00:38:38.616
that is a loaded phrase now
because of who uttered it.

00:38:38.616 --> 00:38:40.384
But for me, you know,

00:38:40.384 --> 00:38:42.953
I think people want
to enjoy the content.

00:38:42.953 --> 00:38:45.323 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think that is
also true of drama,

00:38:45.323 --> 00:38:47.058
of comedy, of all
of these things.

00:38:47.058 --> 00:38:51.329
So as people crave
that more and more,

00:38:51.329 --> 00:38:52.830
I think that's where
we're gonna end up.

00:38:52.830 --> 00:38:54.899 align:start size:81% position:19%
And I think it
behooves comedians

00:38:54.899 --> 00:38:57.802
and people who are in
the creative space,

00:38:57.802 --> 00:39:01.472
to try and, perhaps,
you attack both sides

00:39:01.472 --> 00:39:03.240 align:start size:84% position:16%
and therefore bring
them together,

00:39:03.240 --> 00:39:05.242
or bring them together just
by bringing them together,

00:39:05.242 --> 00:39:07.712 align:start size:97% position:3%
by focusing on the things
that are common to all people.

00:39:07.712 --> 00:39:09.914
And on the story,
drama for example,

00:39:09.914 --> 00:39:11.682
doesn't have to be
anti-woke or woke,

00:39:11.682 --> 00:39:13.484
it just has to be good.

00:39:13.484 --> 00:39:15.319
And the problem, certainly,
I dunno about this country,

00:39:15.319 --> 00:39:18.789 align:start size:97% position:3%
but in the UK, with comedy,
it just got ruined by,

00:39:18.789 --> 00:39:22.026
you know, Mock the Week,
which was a huge show,

00:39:22.026 --> 00:39:23.661 align:start size:84% position:16%
The Mash Report,
which was a huge show,

00:39:23.661 --> 00:39:25.262 align:start size:81% position:19%
that I used to
write on actually.

00:39:25.262 --> 00:39:28.733
They both got destroyed by being

00:39:28.733 --> 00:39:30.768 align:start size:84% position:16%
excessively political
in one direction,

00:39:30.768 --> 00:39:34.038
and also by an artificial
focus on people's faces

00:39:34.038 --> 00:39:35.906
instead of how good
they were at writing

00:39:35.906 --> 00:39:37.875
or performing or whatever.

00:39:37.875 --> 00:39:41.312
So I think part of the answer
just lies into not going back,

00:39:41.312 --> 00:39:42.680
but going forward to a place

00:39:42.680 --> 00:39:45.750 align:start size:88% position:13%
where not everything has
to be about politics.

00:39:45.750 --> 00:39:47.351
And I think that's part of it.

00:39:47.351 --> 00:39:51.922 align:start position:0%
However, you know, I was on
Michael Malice's show recently,

00:39:51.922 --> 00:39:55.693 align:start position:0%
and he, you know, I was
talking about how I'm concerned

00:39:55.693 --> 00:39:56.994 align:start size:84% position:16%
about what's happening
in this country,

00:39:56.994 --> 00:39:58.496 align:start size:84% position:16%
just as an outsider
observing it,

00:39:58.496 --> 00:40:00.264 align:start size:84% position:16%
about the heatedness
of everything.

00:40:01.832 --> 00:40:04.335
And he said, "Well
look, you're right.

00:40:04.335 --> 00:40:06.670
But I don't think there's
a pressure valve release

00:40:06.670 --> 00:40:09.373 align:start size:97% position:3%
that's gonna happen because,
you know, if Trump runs,

00:40:09.373 --> 00:40:12.376 align:start size:84% position:16%
the heat is gonna
be higher, and what,

00:40:12.376 --> 00:40:14.678
they're gonna stop
calling him fascist?"

00:40:15.713 --> 00:40:16.947
So it's difficult.

00:40:16.947 --> 00:40:18.516
I think culturally
what we gotta do

00:40:18.516 --> 00:40:20.518 align:start size:81% position:19%
is play to the
80% in the middle,

00:40:20.518 --> 00:40:22.420
who don't care about either.

00:40:22.420 --> 00:40:23.821
- Right.

00:40:23.821 --> 00:40:25.322
Malice has sat in
that very chair

00:40:25.322 --> 00:40:26.824
and said something very similar.

00:40:26.824 --> 00:40:28.159 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's funny, because
he oscillates,

00:40:28.159 --> 00:40:29.727
I think, between
that black pill,

00:40:29.727 --> 00:40:31.829 align:start size:88% position:13%
and the book, obviously,
was "The White Pill".

00:40:31.829 --> 00:40:33.030
- Yeah.

00:40:33.030 --> 00:40:34.832 align:start size:88% position:13%
- It seems to me we
just have to figure out

00:40:34.832 --> 00:40:37.168
how to build new things
and separate from them.

00:40:37.168 --> 00:40:39.670
But I agree with Malice,
they're never gonna stop.

00:40:39.670 --> 00:40:42.239
The question is, can
we build fast enough

00:40:42.239 --> 00:40:45.643 align:start size:97% position:3%
to have lasting things
before they take everything

00:40:45.643 --> 00:40:49.280
that was good from
you and good from us?

00:40:49.280 --> 00:40:50.848
- Yeah.

00:40:50.848 --> 00:40:54.585
And the one thing I'm really
trying to think about a lot,

00:40:54.585 --> 00:40:57.621 align:start position:0%
and I think be becoming a father
really helped me with this,

00:40:57.621 --> 00:41:00.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
to become a little bit
more empathetic to people.

00:41:02.026 --> 00:41:03.794 align:start size:84% position:16%
We were young and
stupid once as well.

00:41:03.794 --> 00:41:07.231
And these woke kids, they
don't know any better.

00:41:07.231 --> 00:41:10.468 align:start position:0%
I think we have to remember
that they're open to persuasion.

00:41:10.468 --> 00:41:12.269
You know, I don't know if you
saw my Oxford Union speech?

00:41:12.269 --> 00:41:13.571
- That's the other clip
that I want to go to.

00:41:13.571 --> 00:41:14.772
- That's the other clip, right.

00:41:14.772 --> 00:41:17.241 align:start size:88% position:13%
So I really tried to
speak to people in a way

00:41:17.241 --> 00:41:19.410
so that they could hear.

00:41:19.410 --> 00:41:22.680
And I think that's also part
of what we've gotta be doing.

00:41:22.680 --> 00:41:26.450 align:start size:97% position:3%
I think we have to be less
partisan ourselves. We all do.

00:41:26.450 --> 00:41:28.118
We all do.

00:41:28.118 --> 00:41:29.353
And I think there are things

00:41:29.353 --> 00:41:30.821 align:start size:84% position:16%
that I agree with
left-wing people on,

00:41:30.821 --> 00:41:32.990 align:start position:0%
and there are things that I
agree with right-wing people on.

00:41:32.990 --> 00:41:36.393
And I try to just find that
middle and speak to them.

00:41:36.393 --> 00:41:38.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
And one of the things
that therefore happens is,

00:41:38.762 --> 00:41:40.598 align:start size:88% position:13%
I kind of
deliberately, actually,

00:41:40.598 --> 00:41:43.467 align:start size:88% position:13%
piss off elements of our
audience, we both do,

00:41:43.467 --> 00:41:47.638
on purpose, to sort of,
to prune the extremists.

00:41:47.638 --> 00:41:52.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think that's the way
you culturally do that.

00:41:52.009 --> 00:41:55.779 align:start size:97% position:3%
Whether our politics can
survive the social media age,

00:41:55.779 --> 00:41:57.014 align:start size:88% position:13%
that's a very
different conversation.

00:41:57.014 --> 00:41:58.549
- Right.

00:41:58.549 --> 00:42:00.084
It's interesting, because
when I was going through

00:42:00.084 --> 00:42:01.552
my political awakening and
the show was taking off,

00:42:01.552 --> 00:42:02.987 align:start position:0%
and then I suddenly had all
these lefties who once loved me

00:42:02.987 --> 00:42:05.923 align:start size:97% position:3%
now telling me I was a
sellout and all this stuff,

00:42:05.923 --> 00:42:07.958 align:start size:84% position:16%
it was like, you
mean I'm selling out

00:42:07.958 --> 00:42:12.129
to just get endless hate and
like traverse this new area

00:42:12.129 --> 00:42:14.098
that I don't know what
the hell's gonna happen?

00:42:14.098 --> 00:42:17.201 align:start position:0%
Now there's this whole obviously
sort of anti-woke thing,

00:42:17.201 --> 00:42:19.203 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I was just like
walking into the dark.

00:42:19.203 --> 00:42:20.971
Like, I don't know if any
of this is gonna work,

00:42:20.971 --> 00:42:22.373
I'm just doing what I think.

00:42:22.373 --> 00:42:23.974
But usually people's,

00:42:25.376 --> 00:42:27.011 align:start size:97% position:3%
people have a way of going
after your motives, let's say.

00:42:27.011 --> 00:42:28.979 align:start size:81% position:19%
- You know, what's
interesting is,

00:42:28.979 --> 00:42:30.881 align:start size:97% position:3%
the more you become a
public figure to any extent,

00:42:30.881 --> 00:42:33.317 align:start size:84% position:16%
the more you realize
how ridiculous

00:42:33.317 --> 00:42:36.554 align:start size:84% position:16%
what you think about
other people is.

00:42:36.554 --> 00:42:38.389
Like, "I know what
Dave Rubin thinks."

00:42:38.389 --> 00:42:39.857
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:42:39.857 --> 00:42:41.692
- You know, I know you get a
lot of shit, because, you know,

00:42:41.692 --> 00:42:43.527 align:start size:84% position:16%
you kind of, you
were, you started out,

00:42:43.527 --> 00:42:46.630
I'm on the left, and
now you, you know,

00:42:46.630 --> 00:42:49.199
you picked a team, to
some extent, right,

00:42:49.199 --> 00:42:50.901 align:start size:88% position:13%
in terms of politically
at least, right?

00:42:50.901 --> 00:42:53.604
- I think you gotta pick a
team to make things happen.

00:42:53.604 --> 00:42:54.905
Absolutely. Yeah.

00:42:54.905 --> 00:42:56.407
- And you're perfectly
entitled to the view.

00:42:56.407 --> 00:42:58.042
But what's more,

00:42:58.042 --> 00:43:00.077
I don't understand why
people can't understand

00:43:00.077 --> 00:43:02.613
that people change their mind
over time and over experience.

00:43:02.613 --> 00:43:05.883
I imagine it is not uncommon
for someone who starts out

00:43:05.883 --> 00:43:08.552
and builds a very
successful business

00:43:08.552 --> 00:43:11.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
to become more right-wing
on the economy.

00:43:11.855 --> 00:43:14.625
I mean, the more tax you
pay, the more it hurts.

00:43:14.625 --> 00:43:15.559
- You know, 100%.

00:43:15.559 --> 00:43:16.827
I used to say this all the time,

00:43:16.827 --> 00:43:19.196
that my life was an
example of the ideas

00:43:19.196 --> 00:43:20.397
that I was talking
about on the show.

00:43:20.397 --> 00:43:21.665
'Cause I agree with you.

00:43:21.665 --> 00:43:22.900
I wasn't an expert in
a lot of these things,

00:43:22.900 --> 00:43:24.101
but I was talking to Jordan,

00:43:24.101 --> 00:43:26.403
and I was talking to
Sam and all these guys.

00:43:26.403 --> 00:43:28.539
And then my career
started taking off,

00:43:28.539 --> 00:43:30.007 align:start size:84% position:16%
the business
started being built.

00:43:30.007 --> 00:43:31.909
I was dealing with
taxes and employees

00:43:31.909 --> 00:43:33.377
and all of these things,

00:43:33.377 --> 00:43:35.546 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I have more of this sort
of freedom set of ideas.

00:43:35.546 --> 00:43:38.382 align:start position:0%
And I was like, oh, I'm putting
these things into place,

00:43:38.382 --> 00:43:40.718
but I'm trying to build a
studio in a garage in LA

00:43:40.718 --> 00:43:42.419 align:start size:81% position:19%
where they have
8,000 regulations,

00:43:42.419 --> 00:43:44.221
and I can't put a
vent over there.

00:43:44.221 --> 00:43:45.689
And now it's too loud.

