00:52:06.957 --> 00:52:08.358
So what is mind blowing to me

00:52:08.358 --> 00:52:11.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the incredible
situation you've got here.

00:52:11.094 --> 00:52:12.295 align:start size:72% position:28%
And I love it.
- Yeah.

00:52:12.295 --> 00:52:14.931
- You know, of course America,

00:52:14.931 --> 00:52:15.932
like any country has problems.

00:52:15.932 --> 00:52:17.701
But I love that part of it.

00:52:19.002 --> 00:52:20.270
I love this.

00:52:20.270 --> 00:52:21.471
I think this is a
brilliant country.

00:52:21.471 --> 00:52:22.439 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think people don't
say that enough.

00:52:22.439 --> 00:52:23.840
People don't hear that enough.

00:52:23.840 --> 00:52:26.343 align:start size:81% position:19%
If you are growing
up in America,

00:52:26.343 --> 00:52:28.178
or anywhere in the West, really,

00:52:28.178 --> 00:52:29.713
but particularly in the
United States right now,

00:52:29.713 --> 00:52:32.182
you are the luckiest person
in the history of humanity.

00:52:32.182 --> 00:52:34.818
And people, and the reason
we are where we are, Dave,

00:52:34.818 --> 00:52:36.286
is people have forgotten that.

00:52:36.286 --> 00:52:38.622 align:start size:97% position:3%
And it's become an
unfashionable thing to say,

00:52:38.622 --> 00:52:40.423
and a dangerous thing to
say for some, you know,

00:52:40.423 --> 00:52:43.560 align:start size:97% position:3%
some people feel really
sort of shy about saying it.

00:52:43.560 --> 00:52:44.961
And I, that's why as,

00:52:44.961 --> 00:52:48.131
as speaking as a first
generation immigrant,

00:52:48.131 --> 00:52:50.267
you know, I feel a duty.

00:52:50.267 --> 00:52:51.801
- Yeah.

00:52:51.801 --> 00:52:53.436
- I feel a genuine duty
to remind people of that.

00:52:53.436 --> 00:52:54.905
- Yeah.

00:52:54.905 --> 00:52:56.106 align:start size:97% position:3%
Trust me, you spend a
little more time in Florida

00:52:56.106 --> 00:52:57.574 align:start size:84% position:16%
with some of the
Cubans who, you know,

00:52:57.574 --> 00:53:00.076 align:start size:88% position:13%
fled Castro or their
parents did or whatever,

00:53:00.076 --> 00:53:02.546 align:start size:84% position:16%
it's like these people
free, they'll be,

00:53:02.546 --> 00:53:04.948 align:start size:97% position:3%
by the time you spend the
24 hours here, you're gonna,

00:53:04.948 --> 00:53:06.583 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's gonna be in you even
more, let's put it that way.

00:53:06.583 --> 00:53:07.984 align:start size:84% position:16%
- As Francis always
says, you know,

00:53:07.984 --> 00:53:09.553
"Communism is a great red pill."

00:53:09.553 --> 00:53:11.321
- Yeah. That's probably
the ultimate red pill.

00:53:11.321 --> 00:53:12.589
- Yeah.

00:53:12.589 --> 00:53:13.857
- What else has been
on your mind lately?

00:53:13.857 --> 00:53:15.058
Like what, you know,

00:53:15.058 --> 00:53:16.226 align:start size:84% position:16%
I know we could do
the woke thing always,

00:53:16.226 --> 00:53:17.761 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the slight
sort of differences

00:53:17.761 --> 00:53:20.597 align:start size:84% position:16%
between the old
liberals and whatever,

00:53:20.597 --> 00:53:23.366 align:start size:97% position:3%
but what else have you been
sort of thinking about lately?

00:53:24.834 --> 00:53:27.504
- Well, every time we come
to America, first of all,

00:53:27.504 --> 00:53:28.872
on a personal level, we're like,

00:53:28.872 --> 00:53:31.541
"Okay, we gotta come
and come", I mean,

00:53:31.541 --> 00:53:33.443
"We gotta move here", you know?

00:53:33.443 --> 00:53:36.179 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Do you really feel
that now, you feel that,

00:53:36.179 --> 00:53:38.381
do you feel that more
as a father, actually?

00:53:38.381 --> 00:53:39.616
- I feel that less as a father.

00:53:39.616 --> 00:53:41.151
- Oh, that's interesting.

00:53:41.151 --> 00:53:41.952
- That's actually the one
thing that holds me back.

00:53:41.952 --> 00:53:43.420
Because, I have to say,

00:53:43.420 --> 00:53:46.456
I think I speak for
a lot of parents now,

00:53:46.456 --> 00:53:49.326 align:start size:97% position:3%
in this country and elsewhere,
which is like, you give,

00:53:49.326 --> 00:53:51.861
you create this miracle of life.

00:53:51.861 --> 00:53:54.231 align:start size:81% position:19%
You nurture it,
you look after it,

00:53:54.231 --> 00:53:56.166 align:start size:84% position:16%
you give it everything
you possibly can,

00:53:56.166 --> 00:54:00.203
and then you send it off to,

00:54:00.203 --> 00:54:02.439 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I mean, the
stuff that they're-

00:54:02.439 --> 00:54:03.907
- Yeah.
- Like,

00:54:03.907 --> 00:54:06.743 align:start position:0%
so that to me is terrifying
because I think in this country,

00:54:06.743 --> 00:54:08.945
you guys are doing worse
on that issue, actually.

00:54:08.945 --> 00:54:10.580
The transition in particular

00:54:10.580 --> 00:54:12.949 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the sexualization
of children.

00:54:12.949 --> 00:54:15.252
You guys are doing worse
here than we are in the UK.

00:54:15.252 --> 00:54:17.320
- Do you fear though, that
it's just a matter of time?

00:54:17.320 --> 00:54:21.558
I mean, BLM, the idea that
you guys had a BLM in the UK

00:54:21.558 --> 00:54:23.994 align:start size:88% position:13%
where your cops in
London don't have guns,

00:54:23.994 --> 00:54:25.228
and there was no problem.

00:54:25.228 --> 00:54:26.563
I mean, I hate to
tell you, but like,

00:54:26.563 --> 00:54:28.431 align:start size:88% position:13%
go back in three months.
- Right.

00:54:28.431 --> 00:54:30.834 align:start size:84% position:16%
- You might have a
problem on your hands.

00:54:30.834 --> 00:54:32.569 align:start size:88% position:13%
- I think we're
actually making progress

00:54:32.569 --> 00:54:33.803
on the trans issue,
believe it or not.

00:54:33.803 --> 00:54:35.805
And I think one of
the reasons that is,

00:54:35.805 --> 00:54:39.709 align:start size:88% position:13%
is that it's not a
partisan issue actually.

00:54:40.944 --> 00:54:42.445
- Really?

00:54:42.445 --> 00:54:43.913
So your left there, the Labor
Party is not all about this

00:54:43.913 --> 00:54:45.148
the way our Democrats are?

00:54:45.148 --> 00:54:48.918
- The Labor Party
mostly, mostly, is.

00:54:48.918 --> 00:54:52.489
But most, or as much of
the pushback culturally

00:54:52.489 --> 00:54:54.090
and in sort of in our
space and elsewhere,

00:54:54.090 --> 00:54:55.692
is not from people on the right,

00:54:55.692 --> 00:54:58.094
it's from gender critical women.

00:54:58.094 --> 00:54:59.696
Some feminists, some not.

00:54:59.696 --> 00:55:02.032
You know, Posie Parker, who we
were one of the first people

00:55:02.032 --> 00:55:03.867
to ever interview
in a long format.

00:55:03.867 --> 00:55:05.101
- Oh, is that right?
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:55:05.101 --> 00:55:07.304
That video's on, that
video got taken down

00:55:07.304 --> 00:55:08.538
as hate speech on YouTube.

00:55:08.538 --> 00:55:10.674
And then because it was
reinstated, thank God,

00:55:10.674 --> 00:55:13.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Streisand effect, it's
now 1.3 million views,

00:55:13.743 --> 00:55:15.211
for a channel that
at the time had,

00:55:15.211 --> 00:55:17.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know, 100,000
subscribers or something.

00:55:17.247 --> 00:55:19.482
So it's people like her.

00:55:19.482 --> 00:55:22.185
And what that opens
up is the opportunity

00:55:22.185 --> 00:55:25.755
for people who are not on the
right, people like JK Rowling,

00:55:25.755 --> 00:55:28.892 align:start size:97% position:3%
people like Rosie
Duffield, who's a Labor MP,

00:55:28.892 --> 00:55:32.996
to bravely step forward,
and genuinely bravely,

00:55:32.996 --> 00:55:35.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
unlike us, you know, these
people get rape threats

00:55:35.265 --> 00:55:37.467
and death threats and
all the rest of it,

00:55:37.467 --> 00:55:41.504 align:start position:0%
and join forces with others
and actually tackle that issue.

00:55:41.504 --> 00:55:42.872
The Tavistock Clinic,

00:55:42.872 --> 00:55:45.175
which was doing a lot
of these transitions.

00:55:45.175 --> 00:55:47.243 align:start position:0%
I mean, some of the stuff
that's come out in the reports,

00:55:47.243 --> 00:55:48.745 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, people should
look into that,

00:55:48.745 --> 00:55:52.115 align:start size:88% position:13%
because it's absolutely
terrifying, that's
been shut down.

00:55:52.115 --> 00:55:54.317
Now that doesn't mean we
are not gonna continue

00:55:54.317 --> 00:55:58.822
to have issues with it, but,
we are making some progress.

00:55:58.822 --> 00:56:01.758
Nicola Sturgeon, the former
first minister of Scotland,

00:56:01.758 --> 00:56:03.827
where they, they had the,
did you follow the story?

00:56:03.827 --> 00:56:04.761
- I'm not sure.

00:56:04.761 --> 00:56:05.962
- A guy who raped two women.

00:56:05.962 --> 00:56:07.230
- No, I don't think
I know this one.

00:56:07.230 --> 00:56:08.898
- A guy raped two women,
claimed he was a woman,

00:56:08.898 --> 00:56:11.468
and wanted to be in
a women's prison.

00:56:11.468 --> 00:56:12.569
We, Francis and I-

00:56:12.569 --> 00:56:14.170 align:start size:88% position:13%
- There's many
versions of that. Yeah.

00:56:14.170 --> 00:56:16.573 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah, we call it prisoner
onset gender dysphoria.

00:56:16.573 --> 00:56:17.741
(Dave laughs)

00:56:17.741 --> 00:56:18.675 align:start size:84% position:16%
You get to the
courtroom, suddenly,

00:56:18.675 --> 00:56:20.143
"Oof, I feel like a woman."

00:56:20.143 --> 00:56:21.378
- Yeah.

00:56:21.378 --> 00:56:23.847
- But my point is,
that is being aired,

00:56:23.847 --> 00:56:25.348
it is being talked about,

00:56:25.348 --> 00:56:28.885 align:start position:0%
it is being discussed on
mainstream television properly.

00:56:28.885 --> 00:56:30.587
And we are making progress.

00:56:30.587 --> 00:56:32.489
It doesn't mean we don't
have a long way to go.

00:56:32.489 --> 00:56:36.259
But I fear that, my
concern with the way

00:56:36.259 --> 00:56:39.062
that this issue is being
discussed in this country,

00:56:39.062 --> 00:56:41.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I say this as an
outsider, what do I know?

00:56:41.097 --> 00:56:44.467 align:start size:88% position:13%
But it's just, if enough
people keep saying

00:56:44.467 --> 00:56:46.603
the libs are transing the kids,

00:56:46.603 --> 00:56:48.571
you're gonna get
to a position where

00:56:48.571 --> 00:56:50.206
that makes it difficult
for left-wing people

00:56:50.206 --> 00:56:52.275 align:start size:88% position:13%
to step forward and
talk about this as well.

00:56:52.275 --> 00:56:53.209 align:start size:97% position:3%
Do you see what I'm saying?
- Mm hm.

00:56:53.209 --> 00:56:55.078
- And I think because of that,

00:56:55.078 --> 00:56:56.613 align:start size:84% position:16%
we're actually making
better progress

00:56:56.613 --> 00:56:59.249
on that particular issue than
you guys are in this country.

00:56:59.249 --> 00:57:01.351
So that issue is the main one

00:57:01.351 --> 00:57:03.653 align:start size:97% position:3%
that's holding me back
actually about moving here.

00:57:03.653 --> 00:57:05.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the thing I love
about it is, you know, if-

00:57:05.822 --> 00:57:07.023
- Well, I wouldn't
worry about that,

00:57:07.023 --> 00:57:08.258
because there'll
be plenty of states

00:57:08.258 --> 00:57:09.192 align:start size:81% position:19%
where your kids
will be just fine.

00:57:09.192 --> 00:57:11.294
- Well, exactly. Florida.

00:57:11.294 --> 00:57:13.696
As long as it stays purple.

00:57:13.696 --> 00:57:15.498
- No, we're red as red.

00:57:15.498 --> 00:57:16.699
- You're all red now.

00:57:16.699 --> 00:57:17.734 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Florida's basically
the reddest state

00:57:17.734 --> 00:57:18.968
in the country in some ways.

00:57:18.968 --> 00:57:20.637
I mean, DeSantis
won by 20 points.

00:57:20.637 --> 00:57:22.038
Super majorities on both sides,

00:57:22.038 --> 00:57:23.273 align:start size:84% position:16%
and nobody's coming
for the gays,

00:57:23.273 --> 00:57:25.275
nobody's coming for
the black people.

00:57:25.275 --> 00:57:26.376
It's just fine here.

00:57:26.376 --> 00:57:27.444 align:start size:84% position:16%
- That's reassuring.
- Yeah.

00:57:27.444 --> 00:57:28.378
- And so...

00:57:28.378 --> 00:57:29.879
(Dave and Konstantin chuckle)

00:57:29.879 --> 00:57:31.548
- I feel like I'm sitting on
the board of tourism here.

00:57:31.548 --> 00:57:32.382 align:start size:72% position:28%
- Yeah.
- You know?

00:57:32.382 --> 00:57:33.316
- No, you like it here.

00:57:33.316 --> 00:57:34.684
- You're not black or gay.

00:57:34.684 --> 00:57:35.919 align:start size:97% position:3%
- You like it here.
- You can still be okay here.

00:57:35.919 --> 00:57:37.387
- I don't think I
can handle, I mean,

00:57:37.387 --> 00:57:38.188 align:start size:97% position:3%
how you boys get any work done
on the sea I have no idea.

00:57:38.188 --> 00:57:39.789
But, my point is,

00:57:39.789 --> 00:57:44.093
apart from my concerns about
what's happening to children,

00:57:44.093 --> 00:57:45.562
this country's great.

00:57:45.562 --> 00:57:46.663
It's great.

00:57:46.663 --> 00:57:48.164
You wanna build a business?

00:57:48.164 --> 00:57:49.432
Sure, go for it.

00:57:49.432 --> 00:57:50.433
You wanna do this?
Sure, we'll help.

00:57:50.433 --> 00:57:51.734
Like that's the attitude.

00:57:51.734 --> 00:57:53.903
And that to me is the
most inspiring thing.

00:57:53.903 --> 00:57:56.005 align:start size:97% position:3%
And that's, this isn't me,
you know, shitting on Britain,

00:57:56.005 --> 00:57:57.440
because I love Britain too.

00:57:57.440 --> 00:58:01.311 align:start size:97% position:3%
But my temperament, I
think, is more suited here.

00:58:01.311 --> 00:58:04.280
So I see probably in
the next five years

00:58:04.280 --> 00:58:05.215
we're gonna end up here.

00:58:05.215 --> 00:58:06.649
So that's on a personal level.

00:58:06.649 --> 00:58:08.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
In terms of sort of
societally and culturally,

00:58:08.651 --> 00:58:10.153
we talked about it already.

00:58:10.153 --> 00:58:12.255
We're gonna have to work out
what to do about social media.

00:58:12.255 --> 00:58:13.456
- [Dave] Yep.

00:58:13.456 --> 00:58:15.124
- And that's a really tough one.

00:58:15.124 --> 00:58:16.125
That's a really,
really tough one.

00:58:16.125 --> 00:58:17.694
- Let me ask you
one other thing,

00:58:17.694 --> 00:58:19.896
which is that I just
finished watching,

00:58:19.896 --> 00:58:22.332
I think it's Season
5 of "The Crown".

00:58:22.332 --> 00:58:23.666
First off, did you
watch "The Crown."

00:58:23.666 --> 00:58:24.934 align:start size:88% position:13%
- No.
- It will be irrelevant.

00:58:24.934 --> 00:58:26.102
You'll know enough
about the monarchy

00:58:26.102 --> 00:58:27.437 align:start size:84% position:16%
to be able to
answer my question.

00:58:27.437 --> 00:58:29.873 align:start size:84% position:16%
I really enjoyed the
show, and what I,

00:58:29.873 --> 00:58:33.943
putting aside any of the
specifics of the episodes,

00:58:33.943 --> 00:58:38.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
this idea that the
monarchy exists over time,

00:58:38.681 --> 00:58:40.216 align:start size:84% position:16%
and that it is
constantly, I mean,

00:58:40.216 --> 00:58:42.752
the whole point of the show
is it's the constant battle

00:58:42.752 --> 00:58:46.189 align:start size:84% position:16%
between modernization
and conservatism,

00:58:46.189 --> 00:58:48.157
and that something
should last beyond

00:58:48.157 --> 00:58:50.994
a Labor government or a
Conservative government.

00:58:50.994 --> 00:58:52.862 align:start size:84% position:16%
And in some ways I
watch it, and I think,

00:58:52.862 --> 00:58:55.231
"Boy, we could use a little
bit of that in America."

00:58:55.231 --> 00:58:57.834 align:start size:88% position:13%
Like something separate
from our daily,

00:58:57.834 --> 00:58:59.903 align:start size:84% position:16%
you've got to go
Republican this time,

00:58:59.903 --> 00:59:01.938 align:start size:84% position:16%
you've gotta go
Democrat this time,

00:59:01.938 --> 00:59:05.675
because it separates
the sort of big ideas

00:59:05.675 --> 00:59:07.510
from the day-to-day politics.

00:59:07.510 --> 00:59:09.279
And I wonder what
you think of that,

00:59:09.279 --> 00:59:11.915 align:start size:97% position:3%
if I explained it in a
somewhat sufficient fashion?

00:59:11.915 --> 00:59:16.619 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Look, having a thing
that brings people together

00:59:17.954 --> 00:59:18.888
is important.

00:59:18.888 --> 00:59:20.757
This is what we've lost. Right?

00:59:20.757 --> 00:59:22.458
And the monarchy,

00:59:23.626 --> 00:59:26.029
you know, we were
in a transition,

00:59:26.029 --> 00:59:29.732
as everyone seems to be,
on that issue as well.

00:59:29.732 --> 00:59:33.469
You know, the passing of
the Queen was mourned,

00:59:33.469 --> 00:59:35.471 align:start size:88% position:13%
I think, to such an
extent, not only because

00:59:35.471 --> 00:59:37.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
she was this extraordinary
person, but because,

00:59:39.242 --> 00:59:44.247 align:start position:0%
you know, people see the England
of their youth going away.

00:59:45.114 --> 00:59:46.516
And I think for a lot of people

00:59:46.516 --> 00:59:49.586
it was that extra
bit meaningful,

00:59:49.586 --> 00:59:53.957
because it kind of marked
the passing of the era,

00:59:53.957 --> 00:59:55.224
and we, it remains
to be seen whether,

00:59:55.224 --> 00:59:58.294
under the current King,
that continuous thing,

00:59:58.294 --> 00:59:59.228
that thing goes on.

00:59:59.228 --> 01:00:00.463
I think it probably will.

01:00:00.463 --> 01:00:01.397 align:start size:81% position:19%
- According to the
show, at least,

01:00:01.397 --> 01:00:02.799
which I think is fairly factual.

01:00:02.799 --> 01:00:04.667 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, he really was
pushing for change all along.

01:00:04.667 --> 01:00:06.769 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Right.
- You know, from youth.

01:00:06.769 --> 01:00:08.504
So we shall see.
- And if he makes,

01:00:08.504 --> 01:00:11.908
and if he makes the mistake
that his younger son made,

01:00:11.908 --> 01:00:14.544 align:start size:88% position:13%
which is to start
weighing in on politics,

01:00:14.544 --> 01:00:16.379 align:start size:84% position:16%
I don't think there
will be any way

01:00:16.379 --> 01:00:18.047 align:start size:84% position:16%
to defend the Monarchy
at that point,

01:00:18.047 --> 01:00:19.349
because the Monarchy's purpose

01:00:19.349 --> 01:00:22.218 align:start size:84% position:16%
is not to be party
political or partisan.

01:00:22.218 --> 01:00:25.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
And once you start
weighing in on these very,

01:00:25.021 --> 01:00:26.656
you know, divisive issues,

01:00:26.656 --> 01:00:31.661
as a neutral observer who's
supposed to just provide

01:00:33.129 --> 01:00:36.432
the backdrop against which
society takes its course,

01:00:36.432 --> 01:00:38.301
then they're gonna be
in a lot of trouble.

01:00:38.301 --> 01:00:40.436
So I hope he doesn't do that.

